WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:09.753
- Okay, so let me start by thinking.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:15.920
Cause that was quite an
extraordinary piece of documentary.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:20.400
If I may say, first my
personal impression,

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:22.080
the impression of being,

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:26.340
having been able to
concentrating only half an hour.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:30.733
All the issues that are
concerned with this debate,

00:00:32.201 --> 00:00:34.860
let's call it a debate,

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:38.670
between the receiving
countries and the people

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:40.740
that come from other countries

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:42.423
and try to cross the borders.

00:00:43.842 --> 00:00:48.842
There are many, many
suggestions in your documentary.

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:53.073
Let me start from my own
angle, if you allow me, Mauro.

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:59.190
My angle is the European Union.

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:01.953
I am an official European
Union and fellow here.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:06.882
And the European Union was
mentioned several times

00:01:06.882 --> 00:01:11.882
in your documentary, sort of
a present and absent actor.

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:17.640
Although what we have seen
represents very much similar

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.470
situation in other parts of the world.

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:22.272
But let's concentrate on
why the European Union

00:01:22.272 --> 00:01:26.070
is an actor and actually is an actor

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:29.040
by presence and absence.

00:01:29.040 --> 00:01:31.290
I will try to be very brief on that,

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:32.853
but it seems to be important.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.060
While I was starting,

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:39.987
I opened the treaty of
European Union in front of me.

00:01:39.987 --> 00:01:44.100
And I will start by reading
out the first sentence

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:46.470
of article two of that treaty

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:49.650
that says that the Union
is founded on the values

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:52.611
of respect for human dignity, freedom,

00:01:52.611 --> 00:01:54.382
democracy, equality,

00:01:54.382 --> 00:01:58.051
the rule of law and
respect for human rights,

00:01:58.051 --> 00:02:01.833
including the rights of person
belonging to minorities.

00:02:03.091 --> 00:02:06.581
What we have seen here
is a direct challenge

00:02:06.581 --> 00:02:09.333
to these expression of values.

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:14.440
I see the challenges on several aspects.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:20.250
The first challenge is about the safety

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:24.090
of these people at sea.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:25.920
Cause this is an island.

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.720
And we know that there is an ongoing

00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:29.730
tragedy in the Mediterranean.

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:32.250
Not only in that part
of the Mediterranean,

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:33.400
also in the Igena area.

00:02:34.957 --> 00:02:39.957
A lot of refugees are
dying trying to cross from

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:44.223
the Turkish coasts to the
Greek Islands, for example.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:50.720
So, this is about international
law and shared values

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:55.590
of all the world, all
the states of the world.

00:02:55.590 --> 00:03:00.590
There is a clear, an
existent law of the sea

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:07.520
since at least 150, 2,000, 200 years.

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:12.810
That puts the safeguard
of life at sea at the top

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:16.800
of every kind of action in the sea.

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:20.460
So it, when somebody is saved at sea,

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:23.157
that person must be brought to the,

00:03:23.157 --> 00:03:28.157
to the mainland and protected.

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:32.370
That has been the civilization
for all the countries

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:33.510
in the world.

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:35.220
What we are seeing,

00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:37.560
and there is some perception here

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:41.640
beyond this lip service to saving lives.

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:45.180
There is always a sentence
that refers to "but."

00:03:45.180 --> 00:03:48.810
Saving lives, but you have to
do this, you have to do that.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:52.950
This but represents actually a refrain

00:03:52.950 --> 00:03:56.860
from implementing those principles

00:03:58.716 --> 00:04:02.994
of ward understanding of what should be

00:04:02.994 --> 00:04:05.040
the protection of life.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:08.662
The second element is the
element that I perceived in this,

00:04:08.662 --> 00:04:13.662
in this documentary is the separation

00:04:14.053 --> 00:04:19.053
between the human being
and his or her rights.

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:27.410
Many of the interviews focused
on the belonging to a group.

00:04:29.872 --> 00:04:33.240
If you belong to a certain
group, then you are welcome.

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:36.120
If you do not belong to
a certain, to that group,

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:37.473
you are no longer welcome.

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:43.432
That belonging, it is not
clear who should decide

00:04:43.432 --> 00:04:46.320
on what that belonging means,

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:51.320
but certainly that requirement
or conditions to belonging

00:04:51.474 --> 00:04:56.063
is in breach of the values
of respect of human dignity,

00:04:56.063 --> 00:05:00.780
equality, rule of law, and
respect for human rights.

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:04.315
Why? Because human rights
are individual human rights

00:05:04.315 --> 00:05:09.150
and respect for human dignity
is the respect of the dignity

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:10.950
of each individual,

00:05:10.950 --> 00:05:15.950
not only if they are
part of a wider group,

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:19.593
be it religious or national.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:24.480
So, and the third element,
and I will stop here,

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:29.453
and the third element is the
conflict between interests.

00:05:29.453 --> 00:05:32.594
It is interesting from
this documentary that

00:05:32.594 --> 00:05:37.594
there are two levels of
interests in competition here.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:43.250
On the one hand, we hear
certain interveners stating

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:45.240
that there is an interest for Malta

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:48.372
and for the European countries to have

00:05:48.372 --> 00:05:51.210
more and better immigration.

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:56.210
Because we need skillful and
even unskilled labor forces.

00:05:56.550 --> 00:06:01.410
So, we need these people
to move to our countries.

00:06:01.410 --> 00:06:04.260
At the same time, the interest,

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:07.890
that interest is opposed
by those, we heard that,

00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:12.890
that make, coincide the
interest of the country

00:06:16.170 --> 00:06:19.740
with the security of the country.

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:22.743
Security means sealing the borders.

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:26.700
There is an interesting question,

00:06:26.700 --> 00:06:28.770
which is asked by one of the interveners,

00:06:28.770 --> 00:06:33.480
why the war ships that are
crossing the Mediterranean

00:06:33.480 --> 00:06:36.803
in front that are preventing,

00:06:36.803 --> 00:06:40.410
that the weapons are smuggled into Libya,

00:06:40.410 --> 00:06:44.010
that has a terrible civil war ongoing.

00:06:44.010 --> 00:06:47.733
They do not save people at
sea, that was the question.

00:06:48.810 --> 00:06:52.470
Well, the answer may
lie in other interveners

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:55.620
that have said that what
they are interested in is

00:06:55.620 --> 00:07:00.620
protecting the country,
meaning creating a hard border,

00:07:01.290 --> 00:07:03.873
separating that country from the rest.

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:07.260
This is not only the Mediterranean,

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:10.290
you may have an equal on
what happens in this country

00:07:10.290 --> 00:07:12.330
and in other countries in the world.

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:14.610
So Mauro, I will stop here.

00:07:14.610 --> 00:07:19.610
I detected these three
possible lines of exchange,

00:07:20.070 --> 00:07:22.670
or in any event, these are
my comments at this time.

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:29.130
- Yeah, for me, as you
might have realized,

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:31.620
this documentary that we,

00:07:31.620 --> 00:07:35.100
I say we because I didn't do
the documentary just by myself,

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:39.330
I did it with Nunzio Gringeri,
which is a great colleague

00:07:39.330 --> 00:07:41.253
and that's a very good friend of mine.

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:47.180
We tried to show something different

00:07:47.730 --> 00:07:49.860
that is in the published discussion.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:53.520
When we talk about migration and refugees,

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:56.910
we usually, this is something
that I also explored

00:07:56.910 --> 00:08:01.910
in my work in the past, a very
emotional image of migrants.

00:08:03.450 --> 00:08:07.080
So usually when we read that, for example,

00:08:07.080 --> 00:08:08.840
on a newspaper about migrants,

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:13.080
we read when they arrive
and when they are drowned.

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:16.200
We never read about
migrants, about their life.

00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:19.560
What are they doing in Europe,
about the detention center.

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:23.295
The only way for these human beings

00:08:23.295 --> 00:08:28.295
to be somehow, to find someone
interested in their life

00:08:28.710 --> 00:08:31.560
is when they finally arrive to Europe.

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:34.290
And we usually call them an invasion.

00:08:34.290 --> 00:08:36.240
Or where they don't arrive,

00:08:36.240 --> 00:08:39.210
because unfortunately they're drowned.

00:08:39.210 --> 00:08:42.330
And the idea of this documentary

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:45.440
was to work on two different levels.

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:49.497
On one level was to show the migrant,

00:08:49.497 --> 00:08:51.990
and they would like them to
come back on this definition,

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:54.330
because we had a discussion previously.

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:57.540
And this is interesting
also to talk a bit about

00:08:57.540 --> 00:09:00.300
what we talk about when
we talk about migrants,

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:02.100
refugees, asylum seekers.

00:09:02.100 --> 00:09:03.810
We should never forget that first of all,

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:05.400
they're human beings.

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:08.010
So, the idea was to
show these human beings,

00:09:08.010 --> 00:09:13.010
not as people coming from another planet,

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:18.260
but just as other human
beings like everyone else

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:19.931
in the documentary.

00:09:19.931 --> 00:09:21.600
In the past, in my documentaries,

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:24.630
I was inevitably also
because of the context

00:09:24.630 --> 00:09:27.950
that the documentaries were
realized were refugee camps,

00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:30.510
focusing a bit more on their condition.

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:35.370
Now, I had the idea to
put them at the same level

00:09:35.370 --> 00:09:37.680
with all the other people
that was interviewed.

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:40.950
And then the most important
part of the documentary is to

00:09:40.950 --> 00:09:45.920
focus on the effects that the
perception that we developed

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:49.350
in the last 11 years since 2011,

00:09:49.350 --> 00:09:52.110
when the so called Arab Spring started.

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:55.150
And we had all this new phenomenon of

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:58.770
arrivals reaching Europe.

00:09:58.770 --> 00:10:03.770
It's how this perception
actually had a very strong

00:10:04.084 --> 00:10:07.920
development in the political life.

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:12.330
And then on the social perception
that we have in Europe,

00:10:12.330 --> 00:10:16.950
you can see this in the
documentary in different ways.

00:10:16.950 --> 00:10:21.911
There is something that at
some point Eric Mooney say,

00:10:21.911 --> 00:10:26.911
he mentioned that if actually
the African population

00:10:28.110 --> 00:10:32.040
will decide to truly invade Europe,

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:35.580
there will be one to 1.2 billion people.

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:38.280
This would be impossible to stop.

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:42.600
And I think this sentence,
what you say is very important,

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:44.580
because it gives us an image,

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:48.090
a clear image of how wrong
is our published discussion

00:10:48.090 --> 00:10:49.740
about this phenomenon.

00:10:49.740 --> 00:10:53.890
We continue to stick to
this idea of invasion of

00:10:55.110 --> 00:10:57.300
something that is gonna change our culture

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:59.742
because we are gonna be outnumbered by

00:10:59.742 --> 00:11:02.010
these human beings arriving.

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:04.350
And when we truly look at the numbers,

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:06.908
when we truly look at the social effects

00:11:06.908 --> 00:11:11.040
that these arrivals really made,

00:11:11.040 --> 00:11:14.850
it's mostly a political construction

00:11:14.850 --> 00:11:16.730
and it's a political
construction that we can see

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:19.680
very well in the documentary,

00:11:19.680 --> 00:11:24.680
both with this strange
couple saying absurd things

00:11:25.230 --> 00:11:28.982
and with these men from the popular party

00:11:28.982 --> 00:11:31.860
because they are perfectly the

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:36.860
expression of the political
effects of this phenomenon.

00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:42.800
It's, I always, every time that
I see again the documentary,

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:47.960
I can't help but to have
a very mixed feeling

00:11:49.530 --> 00:11:52.380
when this strange couple of friends talk.

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:56.070
Because at some point, it
happened in a few screenings

00:11:56.070 --> 00:11:58.980
that people ask me if these two people,

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:01.980
they were for real or they were actors.

00:12:01.980 --> 00:12:05.168
Because at some point, it
seems a bit that they are

00:12:05.168 --> 00:12:07.361
playing a screenplay because it's,

00:12:07.361 --> 00:12:12.361
it sounds just impossible
that they really think-

00:12:12.510 --> 00:12:16.800
At some point the men say, "Why
are they coming from Syria?

00:12:16.800 --> 00:12:18.867
There's no war in Syria."

00:12:18.867 --> 00:12:22.298
And I mean, being there listening to that,

00:12:22.298 --> 00:12:27.298
when he told us was a bit an absurd.

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:32.720
So I, our goal was to
show a bit these effects

00:12:33.300 --> 00:12:38.300
and to try also to concretely
address one of the main

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:42.769
problems that as European union,

00:12:42.769 --> 00:12:46.290
we saw in the last 11 years in connection

00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:48.660
with the migration phenomenon.

00:12:48.660 --> 00:12:52.367
Which is how the political,

00:12:52.367 --> 00:12:56.250
many parties on the
European political scenario,

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:58.590
used something that is just a phenomenon,

00:12:58.590 --> 00:12:59.460
is not a problem.

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:04.189
And that concretely has no
particularly importance on the

00:13:04.189 --> 00:13:08.430
economical, political, social
development of our countries.

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:11.430
Not for bad, at least
maybe could be for good.

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:14.456
And they transformed
this phenomenon in full

00:13:14.456 --> 00:13:16.800
for their movements.

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:20.310
And we are seeing this
everywhere in Europe.

00:13:20.310 --> 00:13:23.880
And unfortunately, I
had the sensation that

00:13:23.880 --> 00:13:26.460
unless something change,

00:13:26.460 --> 00:13:29.220
we will continue to
see that in the future.

00:13:29.220 --> 00:13:33.240
Probably not just in Europe
because as you know very well,

00:13:33.240 --> 00:13:37.143
this has been used very similarly
also in the United States.

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:45.930
- Let me add another layer,

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:50.118
which is sparked by your
own comments, Mauro.

00:13:50.118 --> 00:13:55.118
You link, rightly, the
increase in the worsening

00:13:55.729 --> 00:13:58.863
of the situation to the Arab Spring.

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:05.539
This is another paradox
of this debate because the

00:14:05.539 --> 00:14:10.440
so-called Arab Spring or spring phenomena,

00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:12.259
cause there are many different,

00:14:12.259 --> 00:14:17.259
different expressions of that phenomenon,

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:23.313
in the beginning of the 2010s.

00:14:24.930 --> 00:14:29.103
They can be maybe summarily
summarized by the,

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:32.640
finally in some countries,

00:14:32.640 --> 00:14:37.097
some democratic conscience
that has been expressed

00:14:37.097 --> 00:14:40.830
through the people taking the streets,

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:42.900
asking for a change of the government,

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:46.293
requesting the change of
the structure of the state.

00:14:47.160 --> 00:14:49.650
Although, now the situation is worsened.

00:14:49.650 --> 00:14:52.503
The best evolution that
we saw was Tunisia.

00:14:53.970 --> 00:14:55.440
Tunisia went through this.

00:14:55.440 --> 00:14:59.250
There was a dictator, which was thrown out

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:03.180
and then some riots and then elections,

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:07.860
and then a truly democratic,
although complicated debate,

00:15:07.860 --> 00:15:11.010
in the state and then a new constitution.

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:14.703
Now we are in a bad turn,
I don't know how it will,

00:15:15.746 --> 00:15:19.620
how it will evolve in the
future, but we have to seal this

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:22.620
and where is the
contradiction of the parks?

00:15:22.620 --> 00:15:27.480
Because we sort of blame
the persons that have been

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:32.400
liberated by all these
phenomena, all these explosions,

00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:35.100
social and political explosions,

00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:38.291
for having done so and having
taken their own freedom

00:15:38.291 --> 00:15:41.640
and their own lives in their own hands

00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:44.520
and tried to move in
places where they could

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:45.470
have a better life.

00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:52.100
So paradoxically, we claim that
we defend democracy at home,

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:55.150
but as soon as democracy
produces unsettlement,

00:15:58.860 --> 00:16:02.640
diversions, complications
in the near border,

00:16:02.640 --> 00:16:06.540
the only thing we think we
should do is to put up a wall

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:10.770
because the people that could
reap the benefit of more

00:16:10.770 --> 00:16:14.520
democracy cannot reach our countries.

00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:16.770
So, we actually promote democracy

00:16:16.770 --> 00:16:20.910
and blame them for having
believed us at the same time.

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:25.170
It's a terrible paradox that
brings me back to the two lines

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:28.830
that I've read you of
the European Union Treaty

00:16:28.830 --> 00:16:32.400
because if we truly
believe in human dignity

00:16:32.400 --> 00:16:36.730
and human rights, then
somewhere there must be

00:16:37.740 --> 00:16:41.670
not a compromise, but a balance between

00:16:41.670 --> 00:16:45.210
the need of security and recognition

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:47.940
that human beings have a right to move,

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:49.653
including cross borders.

00:16:50.790 --> 00:16:55.653
Otherwise, that doesn't work.
Our narrative is failed.

00:16:57.570 --> 00:17:01.620
Your reference to these two
persons that look like actors,

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:02.790
I think you're right. (laughs)

00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:04.440
Look like actors.

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:07.952
These two persons actually
are actors in the sense that

00:17:07.952 --> 00:17:11.313
possibly they do not truly
believe in what they say.

00:17:12.233 --> 00:17:14.460
Because if they believed in it,

00:17:14.460 --> 00:17:17.410
then they should show how

00:17:18.870 --> 00:17:21.240
their own lives are in conformity

00:17:21.240 --> 00:17:25.620
with the principles that they
pronounce are invaluable.

00:17:25.620 --> 00:17:29.940
I fear that we, if you
had the time to test them,

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:32.640
they would've failed to pass that test,

00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:35.940
because these are normally
people who talk about values,

00:17:35.940 --> 00:17:40.470
but do not actually implement them.

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:43.560
Because if they implement
being, for example,

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:46.770
a whole-hearted Catholic,

00:17:46.770 --> 00:17:51.720
how can they make all
these people prisoners

00:17:51.720 --> 00:17:55.113
for months with no respect on the law?

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:59.703
Why, how can they push them back to Libya?

00:18:00.780 --> 00:18:05.400
It's a hell place to be
without any right there.

00:18:05.400 --> 00:18:06.450
And we all know that.

00:18:07.320 --> 00:18:08.554
How?

00:18:08.554 --> 00:18:12.300
So, there is a part of acting,

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:17.040
but that hides behind a
clear contradiction between

00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:20.820
steady principles and
actually performance,

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:25.350
execution in practice of
those values that are claimed.

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:26.681
So I [Indistinct]

00:18:26.681 --> 00:18:29.710
- Actually, about this distillment,

00:18:31.480 --> 00:18:34.650
there is something that can be
somehow interesting to share.

00:18:34.650 --> 00:18:38.190
Because in order to keep the documentary

00:18:38.190 --> 00:18:43.190
a bit more balanced, we had to
cut parts that were much more

00:18:43.410 --> 00:18:47.220
extreme in their expression.

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:52.220
Basically, we kept the balanced
parts of what they said

00:18:52.619 --> 00:18:55.330
of, I mean, there were parts where this

00:18:55.330 --> 00:19:00.330
man was saying that this
political era is unfit

00:19:02.940 --> 00:19:05.100
for example, that we didn't
put into the documentary

00:19:05.100 --> 00:19:07.380
because this, the idea of the documentary,

00:19:07.380 --> 00:19:10.737
of all my work and all of our work is

00:19:10.737 --> 00:19:15.737
to keep the documentary
balanced enough so that

00:19:16.620 --> 00:19:19.770
it's clear, our position.

00:19:19.770 --> 00:19:23.220
But there is also enough space for them

00:19:23.220 --> 00:19:24.540
to express themselves.

00:19:24.540 --> 00:19:29.540
And we believe that their
ideas don't need any comment,

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:34.140
because they speak for themselves badly.

00:19:34.140 --> 00:19:38.577
But we, for example,
decided to not push too much

00:19:38.577 --> 00:19:43.500
and to not put, for example,
these other fiddler declaration

00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:46.247
because we had the sensation
that this way we would

00:19:46.247 --> 00:19:49.170
unbalance a bit too much the documentary.

00:19:49.170 --> 00:19:54.170
We wanted to keep, to give
the audience a note about,

00:19:54.737 --> 00:19:56.640
also these two men.

00:19:56.640 --> 00:20:01.640
I must say that I kind of
agree when you say that I'm not

00:20:02.130 --> 00:20:05.370
totally sure if they truly
believe in what they say

00:20:05.370 --> 00:20:08.310
and I am not talking
about them specifically.

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:13.286
There is a component,
a political component

00:20:13.286 --> 00:20:18.240
that we can categorize as
nationalists far right,

00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:22.140
that it's difficult to
believe that they truly,

00:20:22.140 --> 00:20:25.140
that they will truly
stick to the principles

00:20:25.140 --> 00:20:27.630
that they claim to believe in.

00:20:27.630 --> 00:20:29.514
Of course they talk a lot and they do that

00:20:29.514 --> 00:20:31.560
also in the documentary,

00:20:31.560 --> 00:20:35.583
but clearly day by day,
they direct another way.

00:20:37.350 --> 00:20:40.560
For example, we decided to
use this part when they say

00:20:40.560 --> 00:20:43.890
that he is a Catholic and
they say a lot of times

00:20:43.890 --> 00:20:45.990
that he is against abortion.

00:20:45.990 --> 00:20:49.170
And that in these political discourse

00:20:49.170 --> 00:20:50.523
there is a lot of,

00:20:51.570 --> 00:20:55.350
there are a lot of words
for God, which when you,

00:20:55.350 --> 00:20:59.160
when you think about what
he's saying, it sounds crazy.

00:20:59.160 --> 00:21:00.230
So he is saying,

00:21:00.230 --> 00:21:04.803
he is saying the worst things
ever about human beings.

00:21:05.640 --> 00:21:06.473
But there is a,

00:21:07.503 --> 00:21:11.385
that is very Catholic and
we come again there too,

00:21:11.385 --> 00:21:13.260
a bit the contradiction,

00:21:13.260 --> 00:21:17.666
the human contradiction that
constantly comes with this,

00:21:17.666 --> 00:21:22.666
with people that take these,
they come from these political,

00:21:24.630 --> 00:21:28.017
political components that come again from,

00:21:28.017 --> 00:21:30.240
the effects of the phenomenon.

00:21:30.240 --> 00:21:33.330
I would like to to say
something about this last word

00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:34.890
that I say, phenomenon.

00:21:34.890 --> 00:21:38.347
I also, we were also
discussing this before.

00:21:38.347 --> 00:21:43.260
Clearly, and we should also
say there are responsibility,

00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:44.910
different responsibilities.

00:21:44.910 --> 00:21:47.820
The documentary gives some means about

00:21:47.820 --> 00:21:50.460
where these responsibilities lay,

00:21:50.460 --> 00:21:54.480
and it is important, for
me the word phenomenon

00:21:54.480 --> 00:21:59.480
because one of the main issues
is that in the last 11 years,

00:22:00.390 --> 00:22:04.693
we've been talking all the
time of emergency and crisis

00:22:04.693 --> 00:22:09.633
and to use the word problem,
which is very wrong.

00:22:10.470 --> 00:22:12.900
Because this is not a
problem, this is a phenomenon.

00:22:12.900 --> 00:22:17.900
So, one of the issues is
that if we continue when,

00:22:19.620 --> 00:22:23.643
if we continue to address
this issue as a problem,

00:22:24.540 --> 00:22:26.580
we will look for a solution and of course,

00:22:26.580 --> 00:22:30.485
we will not find a solution,
because this is not a problem.

00:22:30.485 --> 00:22:34.020
I always do the example
that if we will find,

00:22:34.020 --> 00:22:37.613
if we'll try to do to
find a solution for rain,

00:22:37.613 --> 00:22:39.510
we'll never find a solution.

00:22:39.510 --> 00:22:42.874
We will continue to get
out of our apartment

00:22:42.874 --> 00:22:46.980
when it's raining and we
will continue to have rain

00:22:46.980 --> 00:22:48.450
coming in grass.

00:22:48.450 --> 00:22:51.363
But if we were consider this a phenomenon,

00:22:52.200 --> 00:22:55.080
we will not find, we will
not look for a solution.

00:22:55.080 --> 00:22:58.806
We will look for something
to manage the phenomenon.

00:22:58.806 --> 00:23:01.038
In case of the rain, we'll get a raincoat,

00:23:01.038 --> 00:23:02.880
we'll get an umbrella,

00:23:02.880 --> 00:23:05.490
we will find a way to
manage the phenomenon,

00:23:05.490 --> 00:23:07.398
which is the same thing that we should do

00:23:07.398 --> 00:23:10.920
with the migration.

00:23:10.920 --> 00:23:12.033
It's not a problem, it's a phenomenon.

00:23:12.033 --> 00:23:14.225
It's something that's always separate,

00:23:14.225 --> 00:23:17.339
always the human being is a migrant,

00:23:17.339 --> 00:23:21.000
and this is not never gonna stop.

00:23:21.000 --> 00:23:25.940
And the only goal that we are reaching by

00:23:26.946 --> 00:23:31.946
addressing this as a problem
is fueling the political

00:23:33.480 --> 00:23:36.813
discourse that we've been
seeing in this documentary.

00:23:40.710 --> 00:23:45.690
- [Speaker] I have a question
about another contradiction,

00:23:45.690 --> 00:23:47.070
probably.

00:23:47.070 --> 00:23:52.070
You have this woman
speaking about insecurity.

00:23:54.420 --> 00:23:57.690
Can you be, give a bit
of the background of her

00:23:57.690 --> 00:24:01.110
because I might have gotten that wrong,

00:24:01.110 --> 00:24:04.260
but is she also one of the, I mean,

00:24:04.260 --> 00:24:09.169
is she a migrant herself or yeah?

00:24:09.169 --> 00:24:11.580
- It's a very, it's a
very interesting question.

00:24:11.580 --> 00:24:14.930
Also the fact that you might have thought

00:24:14.930 --> 00:24:18.216
that she's a migrant,
that she's a Maltese.

00:24:18.216 --> 00:24:20.880
She's speaking Maltese and we've been,

00:24:20.880 --> 00:24:23.970
we've been looking for
somebody speaking Maltese

00:24:23.970 --> 00:24:26.310
to put in the documentary because again,

00:24:26.310 --> 00:24:30.210
this was a clear contradiction
of what they were saying.

00:24:30.210 --> 00:24:33.870
So, basically this woman was
talking against people coming

00:24:33.870 --> 00:24:36.390
from Africa and Arab countries,

00:24:36.390 --> 00:24:38.520
speaking a language which is Maltese,

00:24:38.520 --> 00:24:41.160
that clearly sounds Arab.

00:24:41.160 --> 00:24:44.580
Because it's a mixture of
different languages where Arab,

00:24:44.580 --> 00:24:45.810
in terms of sound-

00:24:45.810 --> 00:24:47.370
- 40% is Arabic.

00:24:47.370 --> 00:24:50.850
- Definitely, definitely as as a pointer.

00:24:50.850 --> 00:24:55.350
And she's part of this nationalist
organization that also,

00:24:55.350 --> 00:24:59.740
the other two men talk
and what her parties,

00:25:01.139 --> 00:25:03.959
it's a minor part in the
documentary, but it's very,

00:25:03.959 --> 00:25:08.959
it's very important because
explain perfectly and

00:25:11.430 --> 00:25:14.207
graphically one of the
issues that we have in Malta

00:25:14.207 --> 00:25:17.264
not just in Malta, Malta
is stronger because

00:25:17.264 --> 00:25:20.670
it's incredible that she
speaks a language which is 40%

00:25:20.670 --> 00:25:24.570
Arabic and that she also looks Arabic

00:25:24.570 --> 00:25:29.259
and that she feel this distance with

00:25:29.259 --> 00:25:34.259
the people arriving from
countries that clearly contributed

00:25:36.030 --> 00:25:40.713
to build the place where she
lives now, where she's from.

00:25:43.440 --> 00:25:44.970
- Maybe, finally on my side,

00:25:44.970 --> 00:25:47.250
an additional level of complexity

00:25:47.250 --> 00:25:52.250
and a problem that your
documentary raises so skillfully,

00:25:54.210 --> 00:25:56.130
it is the notion of migrant.

00:25:56.130 --> 00:26:00.221
We discussed this before
starting the screening

00:26:00.221 --> 00:26:05.221
and but your, actually, your
work shows it perfectly well.

00:26:09.300 --> 00:26:14.300
There is this logic of
migrants as a category.

00:26:14.610 --> 00:26:16.020
All these people that come from outside,

00:26:16.020 --> 00:26:17.070
they're all migrants.

00:26:18.750 --> 00:26:21.690
What does that mean?
Nobody understands it.

00:26:21.690 --> 00:26:23.610
The only thing that defines them is that

00:26:23.610 --> 00:26:27.810
they entered some way illegally.

00:26:27.810 --> 00:26:31.260
Again, if you are drowning
at sea and you are saved,

00:26:31.260 --> 00:26:32.313
you are not illegal.

00:26:33.780 --> 00:26:35.400
Not at all.

00:26:35.400 --> 00:26:36.723
The law says the opposite.

00:26:39.840 --> 00:26:42.330
Actually in Malta, it's very
difficult to enter the country

00:26:42.330 --> 00:26:43.163
illegally, (laughs)

00:26:43.163 --> 00:26:47.040
because unless you reach the
coast with your own boat,

00:26:47.040 --> 00:26:48.720
which is very, very difficult,

00:26:48.720 --> 00:26:53.340
normally you are saved at
sea and brought to the island

00:26:53.340 --> 00:26:56.013
and in that situation
you are a legal migrant.

00:26:57.540 --> 00:27:00.180
Cause you are the right to be saved.

00:27:00.180 --> 00:27:02.370
Then the question of what if you,

00:27:02.370 --> 00:27:05.280
if you have a right to
remain in the island,

00:27:05.280 --> 00:27:09.270
that's a separate matter,
but why is it separate?

00:27:09.270 --> 00:27:12.720
Because in the discourse,

00:27:12.720 --> 00:27:16.340
the logic of migrant
catch-all definition hides

00:27:16.340 --> 00:27:21.340
the other one, which is mosques,

00:27:21.905 --> 00:27:26.905
the word mosque is repeated
three or four times.

00:27:27.060 --> 00:27:28.953
So it hides actually Muslim.

00:27:29.940 --> 00:27:34.940
Many of these poor
persons come, for example,

00:27:35.190 --> 00:27:37.923
from Ethiopia that is a Christian country.

00:27:39.630 --> 00:27:43.833
Several people that come
from Sudan are Christians.

00:27:45.240 --> 00:27:50.043
There is a sizable minority
in Egypt of Christians.

00:27:51.390 --> 00:27:55.650
How can one simply looking at
a person that has black skin

00:27:55.650 --> 00:27:59.643
decide that that is a
migrant equal to Muslim?

00:28:01.830 --> 00:28:06.153
That comes from a label that
is attached to their face.

00:28:07.050 --> 00:28:10.210
And it goes even further, because they say

00:28:11.944 --> 00:28:16.773
that this one of the last
interviews with this person,

00:28:16.773 --> 00:28:21.073
young person, I understand
is it [Indistinct]

00:28:24.720 --> 00:28:28.170
He says, "They don't let me stay here.

00:28:28.170 --> 00:28:29.220
There is no future here.

00:28:29.220 --> 00:28:31.680
Don't try, don't try to come here."

00:28:31.680 --> 00:28:34.980
Because they will kill
you on the road in Libya,

00:28:34.980 --> 00:28:38.710
one understands the dangers through sparse

00:28:39.690 --> 00:28:42.030
bits and pieces of sentences.

00:28:42.030 --> 00:28:44.940
But he says also "I would
like to have a family here,

00:28:44.940 --> 00:28:45.987
but I am black."

00:28:48.360 --> 00:28:53.163
So, the second unspoken reason is racist.

00:28:54.000 --> 00:28:55.443
Is the color of the skin.

00:28:56.760 --> 00:28:57.960
This is the second I spoke.

00:28:57.960 --> 00:29:01.950
So behind the word migrant hides,

00:29:01.950 --> 00:29:05.657
again I come back to my
article of the treaty

00:29:05.657 --> 00:29:07.650
of the European Union,

00:29:07.650 --> 00:29:11.670
is the denial of the human
dignity as an individual

00:29:11.670 --> 00:29:14.880
because we simply don't
look at the person,

00:29:14.880 --> 00:29:19.560
we look at the image we
think that person projects

00:29:19.560 --> 00:29:22.200
and if that person comes from Africa

00:29:22.200 --> 00:29:26.640
and that person happens
to be a black person,

00:29:26.640 --> 00:29:30.810
automatically that is a
migrant to be rejected

00:29:30.810 --> 00:29:35.810
because it means Muslim
and different from me.

00:29:37.500 --> 00:29:40.230
So, this is what I felt very strongly.

00:29:40.230 --> 00:29:45.230
So there is in my view, an
urgency to fight against this

00:29:46.230 --> 00:29:50.520
direct laboring that
has become omnipresent

00:29:50.520 --> 00:29:54.993
and is fueling the
extreme right discourse.

00:29:56.690 --> 00:30:01.110
- There is something
integrated in this direction

00:30:01.110 --> 00:30:02.670
I would like to add

00:30:02.670 --> 00:30:06.690
and it is a way, the
soul of the documentary.

00:30:06.690 --> 00:30:11.690
The documentary we try
to work on the distance

00:30:12.390 --> 00:30:16.200
between again, the perception
that the society has

00:30:16.200 --> 00:30:18.387
on migration and the reality.

00:30:18.387 --> 00:30:22.230
And we saw this very
clearly in this documentary.

00:30:22.230 --> 00:30:27.230
So there is a construction
of an idea of invasion

00:30:27.300 --> 00:30:30.300
and difference and distance and migrants

00:30:30.300 --> 00:30:33.060
and not human being coming
from another planet.

00:30:33.060 --> 00:30:38.060
While the reality is that we
are just talking of persons,

00:30:38.097 --> 00:30:40.410
human beings like us.

00:30:40.410 --> 00:30:45.410
I always make this example which is,

00:30:45.719 --> 00:30:48.679
I don't know if you're familiar with

00:30:48.679 --> 00:30:51.720
the geographical position of Sicily,

00:30:51.720 --> 00:30:54.510
but I would try to explain
to you for a moment.

00:30:54.510 --> 00:30:58.170
Sicily, which is one of the
southest parts of Europe,

00:30:58.170 --> 00:31:02.103
as it's southest point, it's
actually southern to Indonesia.

00:31:03.747 --> 00:31:06.690
And the difference between
a person that was born

00:31:06.690 --> 00:31:09.000
in the south of Sicily and
the person that was born in

00:31:09.000 --> 00:31:10.953
Indonesia, it's just the passport.

00:31:11.790 --> 00:31:16.461
It's nothing, it's not
a right that I acquired

00:31:16.461 --> 00:31:19.953
because I am particularly
intelligent or because I am,

00:31:20.810 --> 00:31:22.680
I did something for this.

00:31:22.680 --> 00:31:26.340
I just was born in a place
that gave me a passport,

00:31:26.340 --> 00:31:29.610
that gave me the possibility
to travel wherever I want.

00:31:29.610 --> 00:31:31.982
And then a person which is by boat,

00:31:31.982 --> 00:31:36.982
just two hours from my coast
has a different passport

00:31:38.190 --> 00:31:42.903
and is alive, is a
nightmare if want to travel.

00:31:43.830 --> 00:31:47.490
So, we are talking about people
that share the same thing.

00:31:47.490 --> 00:31:51.480
One of these count of these
areas, Sicily is a bit southern,

00:31:51.480 --> 00:31:54.390
the other one I have a
passport to give me the chance

00:31:54.390 --> 00:31:58.237
to travel wherever I want as
another Mauro, 39 years old,

00:31:59.651 --> 00:32:03.660
Indonesia, has a much more miserable life

00:32:03.660 --> 00:32:08.400
just because he was
born a bit of southern.

00:32:08.400 --> 00:32:11.850
When we think about this,
realize that our policy,

00:32:11.850 --> 00:32:14.853
in terms of migration
is grounded on something

00:32:14.853 --> 00:32:17.820
that is absolutely unacceptable,

00:32:17.820 --> 00:32:21.450
which has no humanity at all.

00:32:21.450 --> 00:32:26.450
And when we just think about
policy of Italian governments

00:32:26.730 --> 00:32:28.710
and many other governments in Europe,

00:32:28.710 --> 00:32:33.710
also northern countries
that don't take resolutions

00:32:35.400 --> 00:32:40.400
in order to make this kind
of phenomenon something

00:32:41.670 --> 00:32:46.663
that is managed with one only
thing managed is solidarity.

00:32:46.663 --> 00:32:48.103
It's incredible.

00:32:48.103 --> 00:32:52.710
It's incredible that in
2022, we are still discussing

00:32:52.710 --> 00:32:55.200
and talking about the
way that we should work

00:32:55.200 --> 00:32:56.480
in this phenomenon, about
what we should to do,

00:32:56.480 --> 00:32:58.620
you know it is clear.

00:32:58.620 --> 00:33:00.570
It's not particularly complicated.

00:33:00.570 --> 00:33:03.390
It's complicated on the political
side maybe to find a way,

00:33:03.390 --> 00:33:06.540
but on the [Indistinct] side,

00:33:06.540 --> 00:33:09.660
this should not be so
complicated to understand.

00:33:09.660 --> 00:33:14.660
It's just that we slowly
became prisoners of these

00:33:16.140 --> 00:33:20.760
perceptions of ourselves based on nothing.

00:33:20.760 --> 00:33:24.630
Just because we were born in
a country instead of another,

00:33:24.630 --> 00:33:29.630
which is something that
can't define the rights

00:33:29.910 --> 00:33:30.743
that we have.

00:33:30.743 --> 00:33:34.500
It's incredible that rights are different

00:33:34.500 --> 00:33:38.640
if you're born in Italy or
if you're born in Indonesia.

00:33:38.640 --> 00:33:41.573
It doesn't make any sense,
but this is what it is.

